 "beats": [
  {
   "type": "title",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "globe",
   "text": "How did a dying king's will start a world war?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Charles the Second, the last Habsburg king of Spain, died in 1700 with no children. Everyone wanted his empire."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "What was there to inherit?",
   "scene": "start",
   "date": "1700",
   "place": "Europe"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Spain, much of Italy, the southern Netherlands, and a huge empire overseas."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And whom did he leave it to?",
   "scene": "anjou",
   "date": "16 November 1700",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.45,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "To a French prince: Philip, grandson of Louis the Fourteenth. Louis said yes."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "Why did that start a war?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "France and Spain under one family? England, the Dutch and Austria went to war to stop it.",
   "scene": "archduke",
   "date": "",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.33,
     1.3
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "They backed a rival king, Archduke Charles of Austria. Spain itself split in two."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "In 1704, an Anglo-Dutch fleet took Gibraltar, in the archduke's name. The British kept it for themselves.",
   "scene": "gibraltar",
   "date": "4 August 1704",
   "place": "Gibraltar",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "At Almansa, Philip's army won the decisive battle in Spain. Then he punished the kingdoms that had fought him, and abolished their old laws.",
   "scene": "almansa",
   "date": "25 April 1707",
   "place": "Almansa",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.4,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "How did it end?",
   "scene": "utrecht",
   "date": "1713",
   "place": "Utrecht",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.45,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Peace came at Utrecht. Philip kept Spain and its empire overseas, but lost Italy and the Netherlands. Britain got Gibraltar and Minorca."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Barcelona fought on alone, and fell on the eleventh of September 1714. Catalonia still marks that day.",
   "scene": "barcelona",
   "date": "11 September 1714",
   "place": "Barcelona",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "So what was left in Europe?",
   "scene": "end",
   "date": "1714",
   "place": "Europe"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Spain itself, without its Italian and Dutch lands. Gibraltar is still British, three hundred years later."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Philip became Spain's first Bourbon king. The king of Spain today, Felipe the Sixth, is his descendant.",
   "scene": "family",
   "date": "",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Next time: Napoleon, and two kings who lost one crown. Like the video and follow History Sketches."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
